#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184170 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183963 :question/id #uuid "2308b4bc-c09f-5f4c-b879-3bb67c92f885" :question/math-academy-id "e-15021" :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression $x^2 - 7x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with ${\\color{red}{2}}$ as a factor:\n\n$$\nx^2 - {\\color{red}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}x\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* $\\left({\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}\\right)^2{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x^2 - {\\color{red}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}x + \\left({\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}\\right)^2} - \\left({\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}\\right)^2\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left(x - {\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}\\right)^2  - \\left({\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}\\right)^2\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n\\left(x - {\\color{blue}{\\dfrac{7}{2}}}\\right)^2  - \\dfrac{49}{4}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1481d4a2-64b4-590a-9dbb-c39d3364bb59" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717386 :question-generator/id #uuid "b55e8d29-467e-553c-8260-f444a4f8a6b1" :question-generator/script "generators/06/0663f2850d921e6a373193b29359229f3f72e2e0d05d1c4b609c07cc331f13d9/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "b4d8ac17-c7e1-58e7-94f8-cd4d7a4c3478" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181480} {:answer-field/id #uuid "c16876c9-e38a-5e1b-8500-72c7d437a603" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181481}] :question/id #uuid "bba4eb6f-40c0-51f9-bd6c-081261134bc2" :questio