llows:\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-{\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)}^{2}+8\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{17}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2209d435-198d-515f-b8b4-60c9562f6bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269560} {:answer/id #uuid "273798d5-f257-5699-8aa9-4f4c2f307f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269613} {:answer/id #uuid "3692e43f-c9b5-5ffd-8fc6-a562924ff89c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269764} {:answer/id #uuid "7a671224-3dde-5038-92af-e145da2474b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270352} {:answer/id #uuid "8e191cef-1fcc-5bb8-9ab2-aa4afff1bdaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e191cef-1fcc-5bb8-9ab2-aa4afff1bdaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270499} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f9eedf2-2e58-52db-8e06-a9079bb28565" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271567}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b33c0ce6-8797-5117-a675-fc9bb0069eae" :question/math-academy-id "q-141552" :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}-11x+25.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+25\n$$\n\nNow, here's the tric