icient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+30\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}$, writing the constant term $30$ last:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}}-\\,{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3266af3-d507-5677-9cca-fe953b9f4291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3266af3-d507-5677-9cca-fe953b9f4291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289322} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d49c639-c1b4-5d1c-988b-463effd88b79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289804} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0a2a9da-d25b-54f5-866a-796316d4daa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0a2a9da-d25b-54f5-866a-796316d4daa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289201} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffba8f81-6bad-5095-8d2a-7a84517eadec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290255}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b072df2c-3382-5adf-80f6-f89bc73cbee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-223640" :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${w}^{2}-3w+3.$\n\n${w}^{2}-3w+3=(w\\,\\,-$\n{{field-1}} $)^{2}+$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{w}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}w+3\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{2}$, writing the constant term $3$ last:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{w}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}w+{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{2}}-\\,{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(w-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(w-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48d23ce9-aa26-5f03-b48e-7b7f33f2f7d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701646} {:answer/id #uuid "5992b923-9cd5-5c07-b9ab-35045f061c96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701649} {:answer/id #uuid "5a585b65-82be-54ee-80ab-e5f2df6076a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701650} {:answer/id #uuid "7e78178a-1eec-5f11-b34b-5047c4d3ee7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(t+\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701651} {:answer/id #uuid "93b296bf-03e4-5d38-a50f-c69fe1a26b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5992b923-9cd5-5c07-b9ab-35045f061c96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701649} :answer-field/id #uuid "e492bbe7-00c1-5124-947e-f614f89af174" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701657}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b5c9b41-1c42-51fb-96be-bf1a1b427a01" :question/problem "Complete the square on $t^2-5t+7$. Choose the expression written as a perfect square plus a constant." :question/worked-solution "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{5}{2}$. Add and subtract its square, keeping the original constant:\n\n$$\nt^2-5t+7=\\underbrace{t^2-2\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}t+\\frac{25}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{25}{4}+7.\n$$\n\nFactor the perfect square and combine the constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt^2-5t+7&=\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{25}{4}+\\frac{28}{4}\\\\\n&=\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square gives the required linear term $-5t$; the remaining constant is positive."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701652 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58de3fa5-d939-5613-be03-65b5fa8d507e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58de3fa5-d939-5613-be03-65b5fa8d507e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701648} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f3bebab-1e50-5720-a5ec-dce188e9e9f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701644} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d59c50a-2794-5ad9-a206-78ebfa891c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d59c50a-2794-5ad9-a206-78ebfa891c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701641} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0885a42-36a1-53c7-be24-4bb60c30b691" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701656}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f9dddf9-bc9e-5a58-864b-3fea990dc262" :question/problem "Complete the square on $x^2-5x$.\n\nHalve the coefficient of $x$, then add and subtract the square of that half. Fill in the missing positive numbers.\n\n$x^2-5x=(x-$ {{field-1}} $)^2-$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Write the linear term as $-2\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}x$. Add and subtract $\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2$ so the expression keeps its value:\n\n$$\nx^2-5x=\\underbrace{x^2-2\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}x+\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2.\n$$\n\nFactor the first three terms and evaluate the constant:\n\n$$\nx^2-5x=\\left(x-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{25}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\frac{25}{4}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701655 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dfc5545-159b-5bce-a928-e7439e55707f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dfc5545-159b-5bce-a928-e7439e55707f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701643} :answer-field/id #uuid "516fe4ed-a1db-55db-8725-094885da8ad9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4898a797-d8bf-548a-b1f6-a918f1274d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4898a797-d8bf-548a-b1f6-a918f1274d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701645} :answer-field/id #uuid "972b0a0f-3aa4-55d1-b915-2c383fe5da88" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701654}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aae80fdb-9519-54f8-9106-0189ec7972b1" :question/problem "Rewrite $7-5z+z^2$ in the form $(z+a)^2+b$. Find the signed numbers $a$ and $b$.\n\n$a=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$b=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Put the quadratic term first: $7-5z+z^2=z^2-5z+7$. The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{5}{2}$, so the square must be $\\left(z-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2$.\n\nAdd and subtract the square of that half:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz^2-5z+7&=\\underbrace{z^2-2\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}z+\\frac{25}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{25}{4}+7\\\\\n&=\\left(z-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing with $(z+a)^2+b$ gives $a=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $b=\\frac{3}{4}$.\n\nCheck by expanding:\n\n$$\n\\left(z-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}=z^2-5z+\\frac{25}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}=z^2-5z+7.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39865d90-2a75-52dd-9942-65128c29cfdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39865d90-2a75-52dd-9942-65128c29cfdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701831} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d6b0b69-8f19-5d6d-95ad-b1e3a0a82ff7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701828} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e904a6dc-cdd5-554d-a1e5-31631da2632c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e904a6dc-cdd5-554d-a1e5-31631da2632c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701844} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eabeba0-0905-57e6-946e-8cbcef9e6a76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701829}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66a8e6a1-40a1-56e9-8118-9a40b8acb72a" :question/problem "Complete the square on $t^2-7t$.\n\nHalve the linear coefficient, then add and subtract the square of that half. Fill in the nonnegative numbers.\n\n$t^2-7t=(t-$ {{field-1}} $)^2-$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{7}{2}$. **Add and subtract** its square so the expression keeps its value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt^2-7t&=\\underbrace{t^2-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}t+\\frac{49}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{49}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(t-\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{49}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(t-\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{49}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square produces the required linear term $-7t$.\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{7}{2}$ and $\\frac{49}{4}$; the sign before the second blank is already supplied."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d95091-c97c-5747-9c3e-c4173f55f185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04d95091-c97c-5747-9c3e-c4173f55f185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701825} :answer-field/id #uuid "07457d97-da58-5e08-9ff6-f78041ebd152" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c956595-175a-51dd-bb68-0044854a2351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c956595-175a-51dd-bb68-0044854a2351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701832} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc94600-d977-56f7-979f-586b8454c760" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701849}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96a4bc3c-9fd8-5c02-a43e-795b51645288" :question/problem "Complete the square on $y^2-7y+\\frac{55}{4}$.\n\nHalve the linear coefficient, then add and subtract the square of that half. Fill in the nonnegative numbers.\n\n$y^2-7y+\\frac{55}{4}=(y-$ {{field-1}} $)^2+$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{7}{2}$. **Add and subtract** its square so the expression keeps its value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^2-7y+\\frac{55}{4}&=\\underbrace{y^2-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}y+\\frac{49}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{49}{4}+\\frac{55}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(y-\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{49}{4}+\\frac{55}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(y-\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square produces the required linear term $-7y$.\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{7}{2}$ and $\\frac{3}{2}$; the sign before the second blank is already supplied."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186701837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdda321d-3b34-564c-9904-0822f85e2a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdda321d-3b34-564c-9904-0822f85e2a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701843} :answer-field/id #uuid "302d6c60-56f9-5f01-a2ab-0ff8daed2ead" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186701830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed2a2c9a-c2a9-5a59-9ea0-e4e7b0bbd608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/re