nswer/id #uuid "1d8a28ff-9d17-5c2d-a119-d28784d77a92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d8a28ff-9d17-5c2d-a119-d28784d77a92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705093} :answer-field/id #uuid "93b3d878-1a9a-5ae8-a95b-c935adf4d1fb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8f3b0f1-3098-5155-8d75-31a4382374b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3b0f1-3098-5155-8d75-31a4382374b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705103} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2e8ec1f-6c6e-50d0-9b2a-5712f1e85596" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "92156a76-3dd2-5edb-8b08-bc24f9d86da3" :question/problem "Rewrite $\\frac{7}{4}-3x+x^2$ in the form $(x+a)^2+b$. Find the signed numbers $a$ and $b$.\n\n$a=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$b=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Put the quadratic term first: $\\frac{7}{4}-3x+x^2=x^2-3x+\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\nThe half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{3}{2}$. **Add and subtract** its square so the expression keeps its value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2-3x+\\frac{7}{4}&=\\underbrace{x^2-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{9}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{7}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(x-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{7}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(x-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square produces the required linear term $-3x$.\n\nComparing with $(x+a)^2+b$ gives $a=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $b=-\\fra