umbers.\n\n$y^2-15y+\\frac{233}{4}=(y-$ {{field-1}} $)^2+$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{15}{2}$. **Add and subtract** its square so the expression keeps its value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^2-15y+\\frac{233}{4}&=\\underbrace{y^2-2\\cdot \\frac{15}{2}y+\\frac{225}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{225}{4}+\\frac{233}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(y-\\frac{15}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{225}{4}+\\frac{233}{4} \\\\\n&=\\left(y-\\frac{15}{2}\\right)^2+2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square produces the required linear term $-15y$.\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{15}{2}$ and $2$; the sign before the second blank is already supplied."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717382 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a3162a5-c725-51b6-9e32-0fa5c1978449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a3162a5-c725-51b6-9e32-0fa5c1978449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717365} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fc17da4-afd4-5ffd-8a5f-ce4dd6afd71f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd5a7902-beeb-5509-bb5a-18aebbbb0273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd5a7902-beeb-5509-bb5a-18aebbbb0273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717378} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1459ae0-b54d-527b-82f8-df4d5ca16cf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717379}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d975efd5-776a-5e85-ae06-55c19beda014" :question/problem "Complete the square on $x^2-5x+2$.\n\nFill in the nonnegative numbers.\n\n$x^2-5x+2=(x-$ {{field-1}} $)^2-$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{5}{2}$. **Add and subtract** its square so the expression keeps its value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2-5x+2&=\\underbrace{x^2-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+\\frac{25}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{25}{4}+2 \\\\\n&=\\left(x-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{25}{4}+2 \\\\\n&=\\left(x-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{17}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square produces the required linear term $-5x$.\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\frac{17}{4}$; the sign before the second blank is already supplied."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717384 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fce94ba7-1e7c-5ac5-84f6-18a0a045c830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fce94ba7-1e7c-5ac5-84f6-18a0a045c830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717385} :answer-field/id #uuid "251080fb-8ea0-58e0-b0e2-2493aef4443d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6df920e6-7257-5b65-9c8a-956547ed43af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6df920e6-7257-5b65-9c8a-956547ed43af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717372} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab4bbe8-7553-5b56-8103-8bce765e7ee5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717375}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f88ffce3-b2be-5e7d-b07a-b4d0d0cf5de2" :question/problem "Complete the square on $z^2-9z+\\frac{41}{2}$.\n\nFill in the nonnegative numbers.\n\n$z^2-9z+\\frac{41}{2}=(z-$ {{field-1}} $)^2+$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{9}{2}$. **Add and subtract** its square so the expression keeps its value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz^2-9z+\\frac{41}{2}&=\\underbrace{z^2-2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}z+\\frac{81}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{41}{2} \\\\\n&=\\left(z-\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{41}{2} \\\\\n&=\\left(z-\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{1}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square produces the required linear term $-9z$.\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{9}{2}$ and $\\frac{1}{4}$; the sign before the second blank is already supplied."}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressions Containing a Negative Linear Term"}]}
